SUMMARY:The Great American Tour
DESCRIPTION:Tickets: $39 $59 $69 $79\nAMT Member Pre-Sale: Wednesday\, February 11 at 10:00 a.m.\nPublic On-Sale: Friday\, February 13 at 10:00 a.m. \nThe Great American Tour is a celebration of the timeless music that defined a generation—and continues to resonate today. Baby Boomers have never lost their passion for the “oldies but goodies” of the 1960s and 70s\, and this unforgettable show delivers the songs that shaped youth\, freedom\, and the unifying power of rock ’n roll. Featuring iconic artists inducted into the Vocal Group Hall of Fame\, this tour brings together legendary performers whose hits remain woven into modern movies\, television\, and commercials\, captivating audiences across generations. \nHeadlining the tour are Jay and the Americans\, one of the era’s few groups still featuring two original members. With an incredible legacy that includes 19 charted hits and 9 Top 40 records\, the group continues to thrive with over 900\,000 monthly Spotify listeners. Their smash hit “Come a Little Bit Closer”—famously featured in Guardians of the Galaxy—has amassed more than 190 million streams\, while classics like “This Magic Moment\,” “Cara Mia\,” “Walkin’ in the Rain\,” and “Only in America” remain beloved fan favorites. \nJoining them are The Classics IV\, renowned for their instantly recognizable sound and million-selling\, Gold Disc–winning hits “Spooky\,” “Traces\,” and “Stormy.” Also appearing are Vocal Group Hall of Fame inductees Jay Siegel’s Tokens\, led by original frontman Jay Siegel\, still thrilling audiences with soaring falsettos on classics such as “Tonight I Fell In Love\,” “I Hear Trumpets Blow\,” and the immortal “The Lion Sleeps Tonight\,” a song continually rediscovered through The Lion King on Broadway and film. \nPerfect for audiences eager to relive cherished memories—or introduce younger generations to the music that started it all—The Great American Tour delivers enduring hits with heart\, harmony\, and history. \nFor certain concerts\, audience members may prefer to stand or dance\, especially when encouraged by the artist to do so. Guest expectations differ\, so we simply ask all attendees to extend mutual respect toward one another and maintain awareness of those around them. Our staff will only intervene in matters of safety or when behavior is deemed unruly\, combative\, or disruptive to the overall performance. \n 
URL:https://amtshows.com/show/the-great-american-tour/
LOCATION:American Music Theatre\, 2425 Lincoln Hwy East\, Lancaster\, PA\, 17605\, United States
